# DEPRECATED in Liquibase 4.33+: the CLI accepts only ONE --defaultsFile per invocation,
# so this separate "secrets" file can no longer be merged at runtime via a second --defaultsFile.
#
# Recommended approaches instead (pick one):
#
#   A) Put secrets directly into the gitignored config file used for that step:
#        - liquibase.bootstrap.properties  (gitignored: superuser pw + trader.password)
#        - liquibase.backtest.properties   (gitignored: trader pw)
#      The committed liquibase.properties is for traderdb; pass its password via env var.
#
#   B) Pass secrets via env vars at runtime (no secrets on disk):
#        LIQUIBASE_COMMAND_PASSWORD='<pw>' liquibase --defaultsFile=liquibase.properties update
#      For changelog parameter substitution (e.g. ${trader.password} in the bootstrap changelog)
#      use a JVM system property:
#        JAVA_OPTS='-Dtrader.password=<pw>' liquibase --defaultsFile=liquibase.bootstrap.properties update
#
# This file is kept only as documentation; do not rely on a second --defaultsFile.
